a court in greece has found the leaders  of the country's far-right golden dawn  party guilty of running a criminal  organization  they face up to 15 years in prison a  supporter of the group was also  convicted of the murder of an  anti-fascist rapper in 2013. outside of  the courthouse police fired tear gas as  scuffles broke out at a rally  attended by thousands of anti-fascist  protesters  the guilty verdicts cap a marathon  five-year trial  with almost 70 defendants  i'm joined now by journalist anthony  karasova who is standing by in athens so  what more do we know  well the scuffles have actually pretty  much died down  they were pretty intense at some point  and quickly after this verdict  was sounded across the uh  the courthouse initially there were kind  of bursts  of celebration and clapping and applause  but then quickly we saw these scuffles  breaking out between far left  activists and the police  as a result the authority struck back  fired tear gas to disperse them uh  protesters also fled the scene and  tried to seek some kind of refuge in  inside streets  but at the same time however authorities  are telling us that these 2  000 plus policemen who were deployed for  fear of violence today  will remain on the ground uh in case  there is yet another flare-up  of uh violence that we saw earlier today  in the meantime we know that the verdict  uh it was released it took  five years to reach this verdict why so  long  well this is being called the biggest  trial of an  anti-fascist organization since the  nuremberg trials and it was supposed to  uh take for to run for just 18 months  but it  hit well into greece's financial crisis  that meant that there were a lot of  strikes lawyers who were  refusing to attend shutting down  the courtrooms there were also  facilities that were not available  i remember in one instance they couldn't  find a  video projector to project evidence that  was brought into  the case by the prosecution also  another circumstance where there wasn't  heating in the room that  forced the trial to be suspended but  ultimately  it also reflects uh greece's very very  slow  uh and problematic justice and how it  just takes forever  uh to get things adjudicated here uh  which of course however has become an  issue for the government which believes  and says in his firm and saying  um that it will want to remedy this  situation  what kind of implications does the  verdict have now for the ruling of the  government  well for the government it really it  spells nothing  uh substantively because this was a work  of justice  and uh in fact for the particular  government the conservative government  this was something that it wanted uh it  was  this particular government it was this  particular party  that launched this crackdown against uh  golden dawn uh so there is a huge sigh  of relief but that does not spell the  end  of um of far-right extremism  in greece uh with the end of this trial  there's still a lot of that lurking  around and that still has yet to be  addressed  effectively in this country anthony  anthony karasawa joining us from athens  thank you
 

